---
description: Security and reliability rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security rules
- Never expose secrets in code, logs, or prompts.
- Validate all inbound data.
- Sanitize prompt inputs and outputs.
- Do not store sensitive identifiers in embeddings.
- Keep auth and rate limiting enforced.

# Reliability rules
- Prefer deterministic demo data.
- Handle reconnects and retries gracefully.
- Add defensive checks around external APIs.
- Use structured logging.
- Treat missing data as a normal case.
